As I understand it, yes {roda prenu} is saying that everything is a person
(clearly wrong).  From what I've seen, it seems like {roda} is more useful
when used with a prenix or {poi}, or when used with a negative selbri like
{mi na djuno roda}.

And I believe the answer to your second question is yes.  It's ok to use
{ko'a} even if you haven't assigned it to something with {goi}.

Think of {ko'a} and friends as like names for things.  I can say "I saw blah
yesterday" without having to explicitly defining what "blah" is previously
(or even in the future).

